  #|# Complete templates for common assertions
  #|
  #|These examples supply the entire program and test document. Copy both files;
  #|no placeholder scripts or module configuration are needed. Install `mooncram`
  #|and a complete MoonBit toolchain, with its `bin` directory on `PATH`. The script
  #|uses that installation's `moon` and `moonrun`, and pins `moonbitlang/async`
  #|and `moonbitlang/x`; the first build needs access to download these dependencies.
  #|
  #|```text
  #|demo/
  #|└── tests/
  #|    ├── demo.mbtx
  #|    └── recipes.md
  #|```
  #|
  #|## The program
  #|
  #|Complete contents of `tests/demo.mbtx`:
  #|
  #|```mbt
  #|---
  #|import {
  #|  "moonbitlang/async@0.22.4",
  #|  "moonbitlang/async@0.22.4/stdio",
  #|  "moonbitlang/core/env",
  #|  "moonbitlang/x@0.5.5/sys",
  #|}
  #|---
  #|
  #|async fn main {
  #|  match @env.args().get(1).unwrap_or("hello") {
  #|    "hello" => @stdio.stdout.write("Hello, MoonBit!\n")
  #|    "fail" => {
  #|      @stdio.stderr.write("error: invalid argument\n")
  #|      @sys.exit(2)
  #|    }
  #|    "warn" => {
  #|      @stdio.stdout.write("progress\n")
  #|      @stdio.stderr.write("warning: using default\n")
  #|    }
  #|    "version" => {
  #|      let version = @env.get_env_var("DEMO_VERSION").unwrap_or("1.2.3")
  #|      @stdio.stdout.write("version: \{version}\n")
  #|    }
  #|    "env" => {
  #|      let name = @env.get_env_var("DEMO_NAME").unwrap_or("World")
  #|      @stdio.stdout.write("Hello, \{name}!\n")
  #|    }
  #|    "copy" => @stdio.stdout.write(@stdio.stdin.read_all())
  #|    "prompt" => @stdio.stdout.write("ready> ")
  #|    _ => @sys.exit(3)
  #|  }
  #|}
  #|```
  #|
  #|## The test document
  #|
  #|Complete contents of `tests/recipes.md` (omit the outer `markdown` wrapper):
  #|
  #|````markdown
  #|# CLI assertion examples
  #|
  #|## Nonzero exit code, empty stdout and an exact error
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ moonx ./demo.mbtx fail
  #|@STDOUT (empty)
  #|@STDERR
  #|error: invalid argument
  #|[2]
  #|```
  #|
  #|## Assert stderr only
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ moonx ./demo.mbtx warn
  #|@STDOUT (ignore)
  #|@STDERR
  #|warning: using default
  #|```
  #|
  #|## Require stderr to be empty
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ moonx ./demo.mbtx hello
  #|@STDOUT
  #|Hello, MoonBit!
  #|@STDERR (empty)
  #|```
  #|
  #|## Match the changing field with a glob or regex
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ DEMO_VERSION=1.2.3 moonx ./demo.mbtx version
  #|version: * (glob)
  #|
  #|$ DEMO_VERSION=2.4.0 moonx ./demo.mbtx version
  #|version: [0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+ (regex)
  #|```
  #|
  #|## Read a temporary environment variable
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ DEMO_NAME='Moon Bit' moonx ./demo.mbtx env
  #|Hello, Moon Bit!
  #|```
  #|
  #|## Pipe one script's stdout into another's stdin
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ moonx ./demo.mbtx hello | moonx ./demo.mbtx copy
  #|Hello, MoonBit!
  #|```
  #|
  #|## Assert a prompt without a final newline
  #|
  #|```mooncram
  #|$ moonx ./demo.mbtx prompt
  #|"ready> " (escaped) (no-eol)
  #|```
  #|````
  #|
  #|From `demo`, run:
  #|
  #|```sh
  #|mooncram check tests/recipes.md
  #|mooncram test tests/recipes.md
  #|```
  #|
  #|`check` prints `8 cases, 0 errors`; `test` prints
  #|`8 cases, 0 failed, 0 errors`. Both exit with `0`, including the case whose
  #|program intentionally exits with `2`.
  #|
  #|## Adapt the templates
  #|
  #|- Both stream markers are required when asserting stderr. `(ignore)` skips that
  #|  stream's content assertion; `(empty)` requires zero characters, so even one
  #|  newline fails. Without markers, only stdout is asserted. Exit status is still
  #|  checked in all these forms, and defaults to `0`.
  #|- Choose exact matching for fixed output. Use glob for an unconstrained dynamic
  #|  field, or regex when the field's format matters. The version examples supply
  #|  two values deterministically; in a real version test, use an exact expectation
  #|  if changing the version should require an explicit test update. Keep the stable
  #|  `version: ` prefix, and avoid replacing an entire meaningful line with `* (glob)`.
  #|  Every pattern matches one whole line; it does not skip extra lines.
  #|- The program reads `DEMO_NAME` itself. Assignments affect only that segment and
  #|  its build, not later cases. `$DEMO_NAME` in a command argument is literal text;
  #|  mooncram does not expand it.
  #|- Every pipeline segment names `moonx`. Only the final stdout is asserted;
  #|  stderr is concatenated in segment order. The exit status is the rightmost
  #|  nonzero status, or `0` if all segments succeed. No shell `cat` is involved:
  #|  the supplied `copy` mode reads stdin.
  #|- The prompt's space is part of the expected output. JSON escaping makes that
  #|  space visible, and `(no-eol)` requires no final newline. Omit `(no-eol)` when
  #|  the program writes a newline.
  #|

